Z||000005||DreXteR||11-08-2001||11:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84fierotrevor:<BR><B>acctuly can u guys give me a list of anything i could possible have a chance at racing in my little 4 banger automatic ?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A Bicicle??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   j/k<P><BR>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||11-08-2001||11:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Master_Sushi:<BR><B>They didn't have a TC in the trannie, that kills a top speed. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Um, if by TC you mean Torque Converter, you are wrong.  All automatic transmissions have a torque converter.  That's what connects the flexplate to the transmission.  Now, it might not have a lock-up torque converter, but that's different.  My dad had an 81 Skylark company car with the 2.5 carbed engine.  It was ok, for what it was.  When he got the replacement, 82 Pontiac Phoenix with the 2.5, but fuel injected, I noticed it seemed to run smoother and rev better, but the carbed engine had more low end grunt.  I'd give the edge to the carbed engine in a drag race.  <P>Who's faster?  Race and find out.  There's no shame in loosing.  Only in the fear of loosing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Master_Sushi||11-09-2001||01:08 AM||||Sorry, I ment "lock-up torque converter". I think I read somewhere in this forum 84's didn't have them. Someone correct me if I'm wrong! If noone does, I'll assume I'm right  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Again, with a stock 84 auto don't expect to win many straight line races. A list? Well... Even stock auto 80's civics (now were geting down there) are probably faster 0-60. Look for non turbo volvos, Geos, Hyundais, Fiats, S-10's with a 2.5, oh don't forget Yugos.... None of these will give you braging rights though LoL.<BR>Maybe look into doing some minor performance mods before you go looking for "kills"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.||||reg||12
Z||000008||84fierotrevor||11-09-2001||01:13 AM||||is there any mods i can do to my 4c engine to help it out a little faster ?<P>and whats a ugo ?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||11-09-2001||01:16 AM||||All GM TH125's have the lock-up converter. I think it was 1982 when they first had the lock-up converters in them. The Lock-up isn't for top end it's for economy.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Master_Sushi||11-09-2001||11:33 AM||||Opps... Guess I was wrong!<BR>I'm pretty sure not having a lock-up torque converter would hurt a top speed though. When I had my auto fiero, my RPM would go up quite a bit when the TC would unlocked. If it was unlocked all the time theres no way I could have got the thing over 100mph.<P>Whats a Yugo?<BR>A Yugo is a very slow car, thats all you need to know. lol<P>If you want to learn about basic mods for you fiero search in the Technical area. Keep in mind not allot can be done on the 4-Tech though.||||reg||11
